course: dictionary
lesson: 13307
title: Grecian: from ancient Greece
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where a thing comes from or what style it has. Grecian is one of them. It means of ancient Greece, or in the style of ancient Greece. «The museum had a room full of Grecian vases.» The word Grecian tells you the vases look like the ones made long ago in Greece.
explain: Look at the words around Grecian for clues. «The bank had tall Grecian columns at the front.» Columns are pillars that hold up a roof, so Grecian describes the style of the building. «She had a straight Grecian nose, like the statues in her book.» Here Grecian describes a face, not a building.
explain: Use the swap check: put Greek in place of Grecian. «Greek columns» sounds right, but for people and the language we say Greek. So «a Greek teacher» is correct, and «a Grecian teacher» is not.
fact: Grecian means of ancient Greece, or in the style of ancient Greece.
fact: «Grecian columns» are tall pillars in the style of ancient Greek buildings.
fact: «A Grecian urn» is a vase or jar in the style of ancient Greece.
fact: A «Grecian nose» is straight, in line with the forehead, like on Greek statues.
fact: We mostly use Grecian for art, buildings and faces; for people and the language, we say Greek.
exercise: «The temple had tall Grecian columns.» What is Grecian describing? | *The style of the building | A kind of cloud over the hill | A pet dog that barks
exercise: «The artist painted a jar in the Grecian style.» What does Grecian mean here? | Very new and modern | Sad and grey | *In the style of ancient Greece | Made of wood from the forest
exercise: Which word do we use to describe a person from Greece? | Grecian-style | Grecian | *Greek | Antique
test:
test: «The museum had a Grecian urn with black figures painted on it.» What is a Grecian urn? | *A vase or jar in the style of ancient Greece | A tin for storing tea | A kind of Greek bread
test: «The statue had a Grecian face.» What does Grecian tell us about the face? | *It had a straight nose, in line with the forehead | It was covered in paint | It was always smiling
exam:
exam: «The school hall had Grecian columns, but our new teacher was Greek.» Which word do we use to describe the teacher? | Grecian | Grecianesque | Ancient | *Greek
